            <ArticleTitle>Assessment of serum ionized magnesium levels in healthy volunteers, in patients with coronary artery disease and/or hypertension and in hypertension alone.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>241-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We examined ionized magnesium concentration by blood analysis in patients with hypertonia arterialis, ischemic heart diseases, both of them and in a control group. Slighty lower mean serum ionized magnesium concentration was found in the study group hypertonia arterialis when compared to the control group. In patients both group &quot;B&quot; with coronary artery diseases and group &quot;C&quot; with hypertonia arterialis + ischemic heart diseases, mean serum ionized magnesium concentrations were higher then in the control group, the differences were statistically significant.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
